WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.652
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:09.420
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:15.472
Unit twenty-three: Hedging and Softening. Today you will make claims cautious and academic.

4
00:00:15.772 --> 00:00:18.320
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.650
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.517 --> 00:00:24.204
Seem.

7
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:26.996
Seem means to appear to be.

8
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.026
It seems to be true.

9
00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:31.897
Your turn. Say: Seem.

10
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:35.502
Seem.

11
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.170
Appear.

12
00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:39.718
Appear means to seem.

13
00:00:40.317 --> 00:00:41.840
It appears effective.

14
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.661
Your turn. Say: Appear.

15
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.489
Appear.

16
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.123
Tend to.

17
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.733
Tend to means usually do.

18
00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:55.247
Teenagers tend to sleep late.

19
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.549
Your turn. Say: Tend to.

20
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.297
Tend to.

21
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:03.923
Perhaps.

22
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:06.278
Perhaps means maybe.

23
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:08.360
Perhaps it is true.

24
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.579
Your turn. Say: Perhaps.

25
00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:15.423
Perhaps.

26
00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:17.045
Likely.

27
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.620
Likely means probable.

28
00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:21.949
It is likely to rise.

29
00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:25.527
Your turn. Say: Likely.

30
00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.205
Likely.

31
00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:30.777
Might.

32
00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:33.249
Might means possibly.

33
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:35.188
It might be harmful.

34
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:37.797
Your turn. Say: Might.

35
00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.542
Might.

36
00:01:42.283 --> 00:01:43.401
Slightly.

37
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.824
Slightly means a little.

38
00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:47.720
Slightly higher.

39
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:50.621
Your turn. Say: Slightly.

40
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.398
Slightly.

41
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:56.256
Cautious.

42
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.855
Cautious means careful.

43
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.811
A cautious claim.

44
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:03.895
Your turn. Say: Cautious.

45
00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:07.827
Cautious.

46
00:02:08.633 --> 00:02:11.831
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:16.331
Visal, make the sentence 'Social media is bad' more cautious.

48
00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:29.206
Social media seems to have a negative effect on some teenagers. Hedging makes a claim less absolute, so it sounds more accurate and more academic.

49
00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:31.956
What tools do we use?

50
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:49.840
Verbs: seem, appear, tend to. Modals: may, might, could. Adverbs: perhaps, probably, slightly, generally. Phrases: it is likely that, to some extent. They show that the writer is being careful.

51
00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:52.090
Why hedge?

52
00:02:53.183 --> 00:03:09.459
Strong claims are hard to prove. Hedging shows balance and honesty: Studies suggest that exercise may improve memory. But do not hedge every sentence; the writing becomes vague. A cautious claim is still clear.

53
00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.973
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:17.231
Grammar focus: Hedging: seem, appear, tend to, may, perhaps.

55
00:03:17.531 --> 00:03:18.788
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.483 --> 00:03:22.841
Social media seems to affect some teenagers negatively.

57
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.307
Teenagers tend to sleep later than adults.

58
00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:29.193
Exercise may improve memory.

59
00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:36.350
Soften claims with seem, appear, tend to, may, might, perhaps, likely, slightly. Do not over-hedge.

60
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:40.212
Be careful! Don't say: Sugar is poison.

61
00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:44.306
Say: Sugar may be harmful.

62
00:03:44.606 --> 00:03:46.106
Hedge a cautious claim.

63
00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.494
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.522
Careful Claims.

65
00:03:51.822 --> 00:03:55.656
Social media seems to have a negative effect on some teenagers.

66
00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:59.247
Teenagers tend to sleep later than adults.

67
00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:03.313
Studies suggest that exercise may improve memory.

68
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.588
It is likely that the results will change slightly next year.

69
00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.203
A cautious claim is still a clear claim.

70
00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.220
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.118
The results blank to be reliable.

72
00:04:19.418 --> 00:04:22.572
A, seem. B, are. C, must.

73
00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.831
The answer is A: seem.

74
00:04:28.983 --> 00:04:30.809
Teenagers blank sleep late.

75
00:04:31.109 --> 00:04:34.716
A, tend to. B, are tending. C, tends.

76
00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.115
The answer is A: tend to.

77
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.634
Which is more cautious?

78
00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:48.538
A, Sugar is dangerous.. B, Sugar may be harmful.. C, Sugar is poison..

79
00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.715
The answer is B: Sugar may be harmful..

80
00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.246
Which word hedges?

81
00:04:57.546 --> 00:05:00.932
A, perhaps. B, always. C, never.

82
00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.942
The answer is A: perhaps.

83
00:05:08.083 --> 00:05:10.930
According to the reading, what may improve memory?

84
00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:14.837
A, exercise. B, sugar. C, noise.

85
00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.341
The answer is A: exercise.

86
00:05:21.533 --> 00:05:24.731
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:29.313
Rewrite 'Social media is bad for teenagers' in a more cautious way.

88
00:05:38.117 --> 00:05:39.617
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:39.917 --> 00:05:54.681
Social media may have a negative effect on some teenagers. It seems to affect their sleep and attention, although the evidence is not completely clear. I use may, seems to and some to hedge the claim.

90
00:05:54.981 --> 00:05:56.783
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:57.683 --> 00:06:03.795
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and hedging: seem, appear, tend to, may, perhaps.

92
00:06:04.095 --> 00:06:09.604
Today's value is intellectual honesty. Follow the evidence, even when it is inconvenient.

93
00:06:09.904 --> 00:06:12.870
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:16.553
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

